Ensure a communication strategy and plan is in place to effectively communicate with all relevant stakeholders at the appropriate time;
Ensure that members receive adequate, accurate and timely information regarding their rights, benefits, contributions and obligations in terms of the Scheme Rules and the Medical Schemes Act;
Act as the visible and credible face of Sasolmed to members, and ensure ongoing open communication channels between the Sasolmed office, service providers, the Administrator and members;
Monitor member experience indicators including complaints, appeals, query resolution, call-centre performance, digital adoption and member satisfaction;
Liaise with the Employer and be an integral stakeholder in the delivery of wellness initiatives in the workplace, as well as the provision of information to support integrated reporting;
Ensure a formal complaints and escalation management framework exists, including monitoring trends, root-cause analysis and implementation of corrective actions;
Leverages partnerships with Occupational Health Services to complement organisational health strategies, improve access to preventative and supportive care, and enhance the overall health and wellbeing of employee-members.
The Principal Officer is responsible to:
